# Ctrl-B, and the half of it that is a decision: where the cursor goes when
# the compiler complains. The shell runs the compiler and hands its output
# here; this session hands the same text without running anything, which is
# why the jump has a golden at all (ADR-0381).
#
# Four claims. A diagnostic lands the cursor on its line and column and puts
# the message on the message line. A line number past the end of the document
# lands on the last line rather than nowhere -- a compiler and an editor can
# disagree about how long a file is, and the editor is the one holding it. A
# column past the end of the line stops at the end of that line. And text
# that is not a diagnostic moves nothing and says so.
name p.pas
size 8 28
push program p(output);
push begin
push   writeln(x)
push end.
draw
fault p.pas:3:11: error: 'x' is not declared
draw
fault p.pas:99:1: error: past the end
draw
fault p.pas:1:400: error: past the line
draw
fault this is not a diagnostic
draw
